<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
    xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
                        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-latest.xsd">

    <!--
        The professional's own meeting link, relayed and never hosted.
        decisions.md D87 (D17's v1), backlog NEW-45.

        A NEW CHANGELOG RATHER THAN A REGENERATED ENTITY CHANGELOG, and that is the whole reason this
        file exists. Adding the field to the JDL and regenerating rewrites
        20260825203836_added_entity_Booking.xml, which every database that has already run it records a
        checksum for; Liquibase then refuses to start with "1 changesets check sum" and the estate is
        down until somebody drops the schema. CLAUDE.md records that trap by name. A separate additive
        changelog leaves every existing checksum alone, so quality's 298 bookings and dev's seeded
        estate both keep running.

        NULLABLE, deliberately. Only ONLINE bookings ever want a link; IN_PERSON and HOME_VISIT never
        will, and an ONLINE booking exists from the moment it is requested while the professional may
        supply the link at any time before the session. A NOT NULL column would make every in-person
        booking carry an empty string, which reads as "a blank link" rather than "no link here".

        NO INDEX. Nothing filters or joins on it — it is read only for the one booking already in hand,
        by reference. D39's privacy indexes exist because the erasure sweep and three screens filter on
        those columns; nothing filters on this one, and an index on a 500-char URL column would cost
        write throughput to serve no query.
    -->
    <changeSet id="20260911140000-1" author="jhipster">
        <addColumn tableName="booking">
            <column name="meeting_link" type="varchar(500)">
                <constraints nullable="true"/>
            </column>
        </addColumn>
    </changeSet>
</databaseChangeLog>
